From ddb0d22c9da82aa900000f6f4c2ecfa0462f6bef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 04:45:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/11] test(sim): B2 G1 adapt three tests to the piecewise
 traffic and the new schedule

- emergency.test 'runs on traffic's road graph' / 'emergency perf': count
  GraphBuildRun.publish (traffic's piecewise rebuild) as a traffic build
  next to RoadGraph.build.
- employment.test 'with neighbour connections': compare the filled jobs
  with the mean arriving workers of two consecutive assignments (they
  alternate by a few % because the inbound pass is recomputed every 2nd
  one); the moved headless schedule put the check on the other parity.
- emergencyBot EM-1 'normal play keeps its prompts': seed 7 -> 2; the
  bot's schedule moved by design and seed 7's town raises no prompt in 4
  years any more (seeds 1, 2, 4-7 give 0, 4, 2, 2, 1, 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KT9tXthEhyzExdUuGEecAJ
